From b1e5c99289f3232b6a33e77b9ce6d2d28cfaac73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:56:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(entities): animate Bedrock actor bones and controller
 UVs

Apply repeating and held position, rotation and scale channels selected by unconditional
entity scripts to custom actor model parts. Interpolate numeric keyframes
from actor render age and reset model pose before each draw. Evaluate
parsed MoLang expressions with immutable camera and timing context through
the shared core evaluator.

Bind rotation_to_camera, body_y_rotation, life_time and anim_time. Keep
unsupported query and variable channels omitted independently so a valid
camera rotation survives an unsupported neighboring position channel.
Script-variable playback and controller state transitions remain outside scope.

The saved protocol 2193 CubeCraft banner requires
query.rotation_to_camera(1) - query.body_y_rotation. Bedrock 1.26.51.1
function 14065a850 uses camera minus actor, atan2f(z,x) in degrees minus
90 for yaw, and negative atan2f(y,horizontal) for pitch. It retains the
native unwrapped yaw range. Body yaw query registration 1421e652f has
getter 14220f630 calling the actor body-yaw virtual function. The licensed
Windows executable SHA-256 is
537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7.

Tests exercise camera quadrants, pitch, zero distance, sparse unsupported
channels, body-yaw subtraction, and animation time versus lifetime.
This does not add script-variable playback or controller state transitions.

Support loop:"hold_on_last_frame", including static poses without an
animation length, and clamp animation time at the final frame. Multiply
bone scale into its base pose. The saved target protocol 2193 Hive logo
uses held root position (0,32.5,-16.25) and uniform scale 2; omitting that
pose hides its banner. Native Bedrock 1.26.51.1 state blend 141e6fe70
produces base scale times interpolated animation scale: base (2,1,1),
old (2,3,4), new (4,5,6), weight .5 gives (6,4,5). Resolve animation
bones with the converter's actual bone-name map so a native bone named
root cannot collide with Java's reserved synthetic root lookup.

Compile retained controller UV expressions and evaluate them against the
actual submitted camera and actor lifetime. Preserve supported offset
and scale components independently with native defaults zero and one.
Native controller parser 141cabf60 initializes those defaults and ENTITY
vertex DXIL computes normalized UV times scale plus offset. Cache bounded
immutable per-draw render types so queued draws retain their own UV state.
Apply this path only to verified USE_UV_ANIM alpha-test families; unknown
shader effects and animation-controller state transitions remain outside scope.

Numerical tests cover held endpoints versus repeat wrapping, static and
animated multiplicative scale, real root names, parser-to-snapshot-to-draw
UV evaluation, camera/lifetime changes and independent unsupported inputs.
A private GPU oracle runs the actual GLSL on a checker texture for signed
and zero UV scales, offsets and four ordinary/emissive lit/unlit variants.
Native shader exports and licensed server assets remain private.

Expand explicitly referenced single-state controllers in declaration order,
including modern script aliases and nested controller aliases. Do not infer
execution for unreferenced controllers. Require the sole declared initial
state, reject transitions and state side effects, and omit unsupported
weighted references independently. Reuse the animation compiler and its
immutable camera frame rather than adding a separate pose evaluator.
Bound expansion to depth 16 and 256 references. Reject a cyclic or
oversized branch atomically while retaining unrelated direct animations.
The unsupported variable.length center animation must not suppress the
supported face animation. Tests cover parser-to-selection-to-camera pose,
ordering, missing references, invalid states, weighted neighbors, cycles,
depth and fan-out limits, and immutable output.

Retain legacy description.animation_controllers declarations in order.
The active saved protocol 2193 Hive client entity uses format 1.8.0 with
face/center animation aliases and a declared single-default-state
controller, without scripts.animate. Dropping the declaration prevented
its supported rotation_to_camera bone animation from reaching the draw.
The final saved pack stack has exactly one definition for this identifier.
Its entity entry SHA-256 is
58cf3b66a2ebe76751415ae7f5f9ad81b44464e5ec987f4f22d6e49639cc1f80;
the containing pack SHA-256 is
13facb13e8f0aa5ac233253e5deeca0e8c294512ca5f02bb7c38a8fd5da5d028.
Native Bedrock 1.26.51.1 protocol 2193 renders its labels facing the camera.
Raw assets and captures stay private; generic tests reproduce the schema.
